  "description": "Grundfos Smart Digital Dosing pumps (DDA, DDA-C, DDA XL) through the CIM 200 / CIM 500 or the built-in SoftCIM: control bits, operating mode, dosing settings, status, measured capacity, pressure, volumes, tank level and counters",
  "revision": 1,
  "source": "Grundfos, Modbus for Smart Digital Dosing, functional profile and user manual, 98473491 09.2026",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Modbus for Smart Digital Dosing, SoftCIM Modbus RTU, SoftCIM Modbus TCP, CIM 200 Modbus RTU, CIM 500 Ethernet for Modbus TCP: functional profile",
      "version": "98473491 09.2026",
      "url": "https://api.grundfos.com/literature/Grundfosliterature-6012959.pdf",
      "note": "chapter 8, Modbus register addresses",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "f8dcee1d72c2ec2c5e3927f23999d7564f18ef234c08f0e7358f792c7e20e4d7"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU through the CIM 200 module or the built-in SoftCIM (DDA-C), Modbus TCP through the CIM 500. CIM 200 defaults: 19200 bit/s, even parity, 1 stop bit.",
    "Register numbers are those of the manual, counted from 1: register 00104 is sent as 103 (address_base 1). Read with function 03 or 04; the control and settings blocks are written with 06 or 16.",
    "32-bit values are two registers, high word first (the names end in HI and LO in the manual). A value of 0xFFFF means not available.",
    "Control bits only act when RemoteAccessReq (register 101 bit 0) is set and the pump is started from the pump or the GO app. Value-change bits act when changed; action commands act on a rising edge and are acknowledged in register 203.",
    "The bit meanings of the status registers 201-206 are in section 8.8 of the manual and are not broken down here; the alarm simulation block (701 and up) is not in this map.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's functional profile; not tested on a device."
  ],
